      "New York is the most populous city in the United States, with about 8.58 million in the city itself (2025 Census Bureau estimate) and about 19.9 million in its metropolitan area, and one of the world's centres of finance, media and culture. The name comes from Yorkshire in England: in the 17th century the English took the colony (then New Amsterdam) from the Dutch and renamed it for the Duke of York. It is not the capital — that is Washington.",
